### 3. What Did All of Us Miss?

1. **Still open in [`OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md#L8241) and [`CHANGELOG_576.md`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w576/records_576/CHANGELOG_576.md#L111-L113) — false universality claim `"destroys FPUL on every FCNVSD"` (`READ`, `REASONED`):**
   * At [`OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md#L8241), the existing prose row begins: `**The emulator destroys FPUL on every FCNVSD**, with the same UB (int32_t) cast #297 removed from FTRC.`
   * Both [`brief_shfcnvsdfpul_f2.md`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w576/brief_shfcnvsdfpul_f2.md) (via Pass-2 Section 6) and [`CHANGELOG_576.md`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w576/records_576/CHANGELOG_576.md#L111-L113) specify an in-place replacement of only the second clause (`"the same (int32_t) cast that #297 GUARDED in FTRC behind a range ladder (the casts remain at :3016 and :3038)"`), leaving `"The emulator destroys FPUL on every FCNVSD"` untouched.
   * That first clause is false for `FPUL = +0` (`0x00000000` is the fixed point of `(int32_t)op1.f`, as [`sh_rounding_probe.NEW.py`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/killtable_20261102/sh_rounding_probe.NEW.py#L202-L203) itself notes) and when `SR.FD = 1` (early return via `FLOATING_POINT_AVAILABLE_CHECK`). Notably, [`CHANGELOG_576.md`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w576/records_576/CHANGELOG_576.md#L100) claims *"the bug file's prose row now says 'spuriously overwrites'"*, but its own **Records** edit instruction at [`:111-113`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w576/records_576/CHANGELOG_576.md#L111-L113) omits that change, and [`OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md#L8241) on disk still reads `**The emulator destroys FPUL on every FCNVSD**`.

2. **Cold-debugger `fpscr=` assignment bypasses [`sh_update_fpscr()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L868-L882)'s `FR` register-bank swap (`READ`, `REASONED`):**
   * In [`sh_cpu_new()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L140), the debugger exposes `fpscr` as a raw `CPU_SETTINGS_ADD_REGISTER32("fpscr", cpu->cd.sh.fpscr)`. Writing `fpscr=0x00080000` in the debugger mutates `cpu->cd.sh.fpscr` directly without calling [`sh_update_fpscr()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L868-L882).
   * Why this matters for the P3 contract note on `FPSCR.FR`: [`sh_update_fpscr()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L868-L882) implements `FPSCR.FR` by physically swapping the `cpu->cd.sh.fr[0..15]` and `cpu->cd.sh.xf[0..15]` arrays when `(fpscr ^ old_fpscr) & SH_FPSCR_FR` is non-zero, so [`to_be_translated_1111`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L5028-L5031) always binds `ic->arg[0] = (size_t)&cpu->cd.sh.fr[r8]`. If a future probe row ever tried to vary `FPSCR.FR=1` via the cold debugger's `fpscr=` setting (rather than guest `LDS Rm,FPSCR` or `FRCHG`), `fr[]` and `xf[]` would **not** swap and `old_fpscr` (`0`) would become desynchronized from `fpscr.FR`.

3. **Unobserved output registers (`FPSCR`, `SR`, `fr[4..15]`, `xf[0..15]`) and model vs. hardware contract (`READ`, `REASONED`):**
   * Architecturally ([`brief_shfcnvsdfpul_p1.md`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w576/brief_shfcnvsdfpul_p1.md#L70-L91)), `FCNVSD` updates `FPSCR` cause/flag bits (`clear_cause()`, `set_E()` on `DENORM` when `DN=0`, `invalid(n)` on `sNaN`), which GXemul leaves unmodelled (`qhshfpexcept`). Thus the product comment in [`cpu_sh_instr.c`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3057-L3058) (`"FCNVSD reads FPUL and writes DRn only"`) describes the data-register / GXemul model contract, and because no probe row reads back `FPSCR` after `FCNVSD`, a mutant that clobbers `FPSCR` (e.g., `cpu->cd.sh.fpscr |= SH_FPSCR_INEXACT;`) or a non-target register (`fr[4..15]`) escapes all 52 sessions. *(Noted in [`CHANGELOG_576.md`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w576/records_576/CHANGELOG_576.md#L96-L98).)*

4. **Working-tree state during late reading (`READ`):**
   * While `#576` is not yet in [`CHANGELOG.md`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/CHANGELOG.md#L1-L40) or [`OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md#L8241) (`:24099`), the working tree files [`src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3049-L3067), [`regress/sh_rounding_probe.py`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L173-L258), and [`regress/gate_sh_rounding.sh`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_sh_rounding.sh#L59-L85) already carry the staged `#576` edits on disk.

